# `## Unreleased` is append-only, so every concurrent branch adds its
# bullet at the same offset and every merge conflicts — mechanically,
# on changes that never actually disagree. The `union` driver keeps
# both sides' lines instead of raising a conflict.
#
# Safe here because entries are independent one-line bullets that are
# only ever added. It would be the wrong choice for a file where two
# branches might edit the *same* line and one side must win: union
# would silently keep both. Review the resulting order at release time
# — union preserves both sides but does not promise their sequence.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
